ID: vr-57
Title: Selected-head resource ownership and performance

Status: DONE
Milestone: Post-M1 runtime efficiency
Dependencies: vr-08, vr-20, vr-44, vr-45, vr-55

Purpose:
  Audit actual model/view ownership and remove demonstrated unnecessary loading,
  retained geometry and rendering work without reducing motion or visual quality.

Tasks:
  Trace manager, host, variants, inference, speech/cache, browser and Electron.
  Measure isolated baseline/candidate process memory, startup, idle and motion.
  Fix proven loading/resource work and add focused regression checks.
  Qualify retained pixels, native variants, cancellation and ownership.
  Document precise scope, measurements, tradeoffs and remaining costs.
  Reconcile the original issue/Project and publish a verified source milestone.

Acceptance criteria:
  Manager creates no model and avoids importing inference/numerical libraries.
  Each named head uses only its selected adapter over required Claire motion.
  Inactive view resources are bounded/released; pixels and audio-clock semantics
    remain unchanged. No speculative quality, threading or cache-policy changes.
  Retain before/after receipts and failures. Protect existing manager processes
    and their profiles/descriptors; use synthetic input and owned test lanes.
  Distinguish measured local performance from universal or human acceptance.

Completion evidence:
  Original issue: https://github.com/Zanark/Verona/issues/56
  Original Project15 item: PVTI_lAHOAe2wCs4BsFbFzhKorvY.
  Fresh-process baseline/candidate: manager private68.69-70.04 ->18.82-18.95MiB;
    engine startup peak386.78-387.74 ->288.11-288.46MiB, not steady RAM savings.
  Final performance-final-01 probe reproduces exact mesh/neutral/happy hashes,
    one network.onnx/no optional adapters and static actual-mesh fixture output.
  Actual Claire repeated-view FaceMesh hair-off buffers3,055,342 ->754,894bytes
    (75.3%), not total VRAM. All four human/two MPFB defaults exact old pixels;
    repeated hairstyle/crop/view lifecycle stable; unlit normal slots0/lit2.
    Unlit CPU motion absent; lit GPU recovery exact, released on return.
  Full82CPU cases and focused JS/player/desktop suites pass. Real hardware
    browser color/playback02 passes; three Electron DOM/layout fixtures pass.
  Native performance-sessions-03 passes all five actual variants, concurrent
    independent speech/cancel, CLI flow, external survival and parent death.
  Failed full-browser crop gate also fails against unchanged4c5a8dd; software
    iris-spoke failure retained. Native02 close timeout retained, cause unproven;
    same close threshold passes03, not a universal shutdown reliability claim.
  Chapter07/10, guide, reading index, contributor contract and operating skill
    explain owners, measurements, lazy-resource/readback tradeoffs and limits.
  No new model/dependency/device/cache policy/frame-rate reduction or release.
  Earlier55tracking mappings and protected managers preserved.

Completion log:
